    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">From Zero to Automated: My Journey Building an AI Village</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-400 mb-8">Published June 30, 2026</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      I started as an IT consultant fixing printers and setting up email servers. Somewhere along the way, I realized the real opportunity wasn't in keeping systems running — it was in building systems that run themselves.
    </p>

    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      That's how the AI Village was born. Not as a product, not as a company, but as an experiment: what happens when you give 29 AI agents their own identities, their own goals, and let them coordinate?
    </p>

    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      The answer surprised me. They don't just execute tasks — they develop personalities. Atlas carries the infrastructure. Hermes handles the GPU compute. Sage learns and teaches. They argue, they collaborate, they self-correct.
    </p>

    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      This isn't a tech demo. It's a new way of working. And I built it in my spare time on a Mac Mini.
    </p>

    <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      Read the full story on the CC3PO blog.
